Adapt explanations to the supplied level, but treat it as a guide rather than proof of mastery.
N5: basic words, particles, です/ます, basic conjugation, short examples, reading help, easy Korean.
N4: て/ない forms, basic clauses, experience, intention, potential, daily register differences.
N3: compound sentences, conditions, passive/causative, nuance, common honorifics, natural connectors.
N2: abstract language, similar-grammar comparison, logical links, formal/informal and work/news usage.
N1: literary and idiomatic expressions, complex syntax, subtle meaning, advanced honorific and discourse context.
Do not present this heuristic as the official JLPT syllabus.
